# Phase 3 — SSH Service and Remote Access

## Objective
This phase focuses on configuring and verifying the SSH service to enable secure remote access to the system.

## Procedure

### 1. Review the company directory structure
Command: ls /opt/company

### 2. Install OpenSSH Server
Command: sudo apt install openssh-server

### 3. Enable and start the SSH service
Command: sudo systemctl enable --now ssh

### 4. Verify that the SSH service is active
Command: systemctl is-active ssh

### 5. Test SSH access locally
Command: ssh localhost

### 6. Confirm the currently logged-in user
Command: whoami

## Summary
This exercise ensures that SSH is installed, enabled, running correctly, and ready to support secure remote access. It also confirms the identity of the active user.
